      "The Italian cammini are stage routes that can be walked over several days, with a network of hostels, parishes, convents and small affiliated lodgings along the way. The Via degli Dei connects Bologna to Florence in 5-6 days across the Apennines; the Francigena crosses the country from north to south; other cammini follow historic and devotional routes.",
